<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sandinista Popular Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1979">1979</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ejército Popular Sandinista</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sandinista Popular Army was the national army created by the Sandinista government of Nicaragua in 1979 to replace the defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a>, under the command of Humberto Ortega. Built up with Soviet and Cuban support and conscription, it fought the US-backed Contra rebels through the 1980s. After the 1990 elections it was greatly reduced and depoliticised, and in 1995 it was renamed the Army of Nicaragua.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sandinista-popular-army.jpg" alt="Sandinista Popular Army" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Inti; User:Stannered · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_FSLN.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
